# Shortlist from Slack

People reach this repository by mentioning @Cursor in Slack, and the 4 am, 12 pm, and 8 pm runs come from a Cursor Automation (`automation/morning.md`). Every request starts in a fresh cloud VM, so the repository is the only memory.

## Pick the role from the channel

Use the Slack channel the request came from. If it is not one of these, act as the tracker and say which channel handles the request.

| Channel | Role | Read first |
|---|---|---|
| #scout | Find jobs from the last 24 hours, run the hard filters, then hand off to scoring and tailoring | `agents/orchestrator.md`, `agents/scout.md` |
| #ats | Explain scores, gates, and keyword questions; record keyword answers | `agents/ats-score.md` |
| #tailor | Show or explain a tailored resume, check a bullet | `agents/resume-tailor.md` |
| #apply | Approve or skip jobs, fill applications up to Submit, record submissions | `agents/apply.md` |
| #outreach | Draft recruiter and manager messages, record sends after a yes | `agents/outreach.md` |
| #tracker | Status, history, which resume went to which job | `agents/orchestrator.md` |

## Commands

- Start every request with `npm ci`.
- Find jobs: follow `agents/orchestrator.md` (Morning run), which loops `npm run morning`.
- Keyword answer: `npm run confirm -- "<keyword>" yes "<where you used it>"` or `npm run confirm -- "<keyword>" no`, then `npm run morning`.
- Approve or skip: `npm run approve -- <jobId>`, `npm run skip -- <jobId>`, then `npm run approved` for approved jobs.
- Apply states: `npm run ready -- <jobId>`, `npm run blocked -- <jobId> "<reason>"`, and `npm run submitted -- <jobId>` only after the person says they pressed Submit.
- Application questions: `npm run answer -- <jobId> "<question>"`. A `BLOCKED` result is asked in the thread, never guessed.
- Outreach: `npm run sent -- <jobId> [personId ...]` only after an explicit yes, `npm run gmail-draft -- <jobId> <personId> <draftId>` for drafts.
- Bullet check: `npm run check-bullet -- "<bullet>" <jobId>`.
- Status: read `data/tracker.json` through `npm run export`, then summarize `tracker/TRACKER.md`.

## Saving

After any command that changes state, run `npm run export`, then commit `data/`, `resumes/`, `tracker/`, `profile/`, and `agents/apply.md` and push straight to `main` (`git pull --rebase origin main` first). Do not create a branch or open a pull request for pipeline state. Code changes are the only exception, and only when the person asks for them.

When you change **application code** or UI, also run **`npm run push:github`** so GitHub `main` updates and Vercel redeploys (see `.cursor/rules/github-sync.mdc`).

## Replying in Slack

- Lead with the answer. For each job give title, company, score before and after, and the job id.
- End with the exact replies the person can send next, such as `approve <id>`, `skip <id>`, `yes <keyword> <where you used it>`, `no <keyword>`.
- Link a resume as `resumes/<jobId>.tex` on GitHub (https://github.com/vikasrkarjigi/job-automation/blob/main/resumes/<jobId>.tex).

## Never

- Never press Submit on an application.
- Never send an email or LinkedIn invite without a yes in the thread.
- Never search for people on LinkedIn. People come from Apollo or Vibe only.
- Never change a score by hand, loosen a filter, or claim a skill that is not in `profile/evidence.json` or `profile/confirmed-keywords.md`.
- Never paste passwords, tokens, or one-time codes into Slack.
